{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794214754,"nonce":"kmkOimKpsaByL7qfVKz2h9Agl7g=","title":"CI: a russl check step for Blinc's russl shaders","message":"Owner direction 2026-11-09: once russl covers enough of Blinc's shaders, CI gets a dedicated russl check step.\n\nWhat a cargo build already gives: a russl error fails the `russl!` expansion, so Check, Clippy and every build job fail on it today (blinc_gpu/src/sdf_russl). What it does not give, and the step should:\n\n- Warnings as failures. russl reports warnings through a deprecated-item trick, so they surface as rustc warnings, and the Clippy job runs with -W, so an unused binding or a naming slip in a shader passes CI silently.\n- Every target checked by its own toolchain, not only naga's validator: DXC for HLSL (extend the existing HLSL DXC Shader Check job), spirv-val for SPIR-V, the Metal compiler on the macOS runner for MSL, glslangValidator for GLSL ES where a shader has GLSL.\n- The parity tests run, not skip. blinc_gpu's russl_parity skips without an adapter that has vertex storage; the step needs a runner where it runs (lavapipe under xvfb on Linux, or the macOS runner), or a skip should fail the step.\n- While a shader exists in both WGSL and russl (sdf_core today), a reminder that the parity test is the only thing tying them; the step goes away for a shader once its WGSL copy is deleted.\n\nDepends on russl: modules across files (russl a2e18cc), so the shaders can live as files and russl_cli can publish; native targets validated against the consumer's binding model (russl 6df56a3).\n\nShape: `cargo install russl_cli` (pinned to the version blinc_gpu uses), `russl check --deny-warnings` over every russl source, then the native validators over `russl emit` output.","files":null}]}